  "slug": "archaea-duplication-d927",
  "summary": "New tools derive repeat, coding and protein-family catalogs from assemblies, alignments and orthogroups without relying on a single reference annotation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is delimiting genomic content from cross-genome evidence rather than per-genome reference annotation. Genomes2Genes converts Progressive Cactus whole-genome alignments into validated coding sequence alignments for extant and ancestral species. The gbe study maps verified protein complex components to orthogroups across 31 eukaryotes, identifies 184 universal orthogroups, and releases the PCOC suite. PANTHER 2027 extends phylogenetic protein family trees and GO annotations across 131 genomes. TideCluster applies a reference-independent strategy to tandem repeats, building family catalogs with consensus monomers from assemblies for comparative and pangenomic analysis. The Malian P. falciparum HiFi assemblies supply near-complete genomes that such analyses require. The items differ in organism, data type and objective, so this is a shared strategy rather than a common method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-15"
}
